# FABLE-SONNET-SEND-REF-20260925-172 commit 4: `sendMessage: Ref X`'s driver-side behavioral
# witness. Behind the driver fact `ref 1`, l2_driver_before_turn (Grok's before_turn launch tap,
# FABLE-GROKBOT-LAUNCH-TAP-20260925-182) builds a standalone peer Message and posts R0 a
# `Ping(n: 1)` letter whose sender is that peer, AFTER the host's own mainArgs letter -- so R0's
# inbox holds [mainArgs, Ping] in that order when its one turn starts. receiveMessage always takes
# the NEXT letter (no admission-driven search: a mismatched shape throws, it does not skip and try
# again -- measured, not assumed), so the fixture takes mainArgs bare first (untyped, discarded,
# the same shape a program that ignores its own arguments already uses) and only then
# `receiveMessage: m Ping` for the peer's own letter. The reply (`sendMessage: m\sender Pong(...)`)
# goes through l2_driver_service_post's own observation point (-Dlmx_service_post), which counts it
# against the peer's address without needing to inspect any mailbox afterward, and unregisters the
# peer synchronously so the host can still close.
MainLetter:
    char: []: []: mainArgs
end: MainLetter

Ping:
    int: n 0
end: Ping

Pong:
    int: n 0
end: Pong

fn: check () int
    receiveMessage: junk MainLetter
    receiveMessage: m Ping
    if: m = 0
        return: 90
    if: m\sender = 0
        return: 91
    sendMessage: m\sender Pong(n: 2)
    return: 0

int: got
got: check()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: got; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
